'''Brollow''' (ツバメンズ, ''Tsubamenzu'') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that appears in [[The Aku Realms]] and [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 4.3 Update|Version 4.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Brollow
|image = E 207.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[I'm onto you|Sub-chapter 26 - I'm onto you]]<br>
'''Aku Realms''': [[Ghana (Aku Realm)|Ghana/Wakayama]]
|money drop = 150¢ - 593¢
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Mysterious Captain|Sub-chapter 16 - Mysterious Captain]]
}}

==Enemy==
Basically a faster and stronger version of [[Gabriel]], Brollow flies at extreme speeds, has low health, and deals high damage that can easily break through your defenses in numbers. He has 150 range, slightly outranging most meatshields and usually hitting his target before they hit him.

==Strategy==
Brollow's high attack damage, high knockback count and full backswing are pretty threatening. Although he stands still for a few seconds after each attack, a few hits from even very weak meatshields like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] as well as the default [[Cat Cannon]]/[[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] can reset it, causing further destruction despite his very low range. As a result, it's recommended to use units that outrange him, paired with meatshields that will at least absorb one attack, or in the case of larger groups, employ specialist tankers like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] or [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to give you some breathing room. While he's standing there, you can use said ranged [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] that deal serious damage to minimize his impact to your unit. The likes of [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] can be used to easily remove them.

