==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Tsubamenzu (ツバメンズ), is a portmanteau of 燕 ''tsubame'' ([[wikipedia:Swallow|swallow]]) and メンズ ''menzu'' (men, mens or men's, referencing his chiseled physique and tendency to spawn in groups).
*His design appears to take inspiration from several different birds:
**He is mainly based off of the swallow, a type of bird well known for its black coat and long, v-shaped tail. Swallows are also a symbol of good luck, fidelity in marriage and fertility in Japanese culture. By contrast, [[Diabrollow]] has traits associated with crows (dark plumage, high intelligence, drawn to shiny objects), which carry connotations of death and ill omen.
**He closely resembles a [[wikipedia:Gannet|gannet]], known to be the "missile bird".
**He may additionally be based off of the [[wikipedia:Common swift|common swift]], the world's fastest bird in '''horizontal''' flight, which can be clearly seen as Brollow moves forward. It also has a shorter, smaller v-shaped tail, though it is still noticeable. Another similarity between Brollow and the swift: the wings are slightly more forward on the body than they are on a swallow.
**While not a bird, Brollow could also be based on a Swordfish, which has a needle like mouth and it "flies" through the ocean.
*The phrase, "DO YOU EVEN LIFT???" in his description is a reference to [http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/do-you-even-lift a meme of the same name].
*His Japanese description references the [https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ToastOfTardiness Toast of Tardiness] trope, wherein (usually female) students who are late to school run there with toast in their mouth. On the way, they may meet someone else by bumping into them, just like Brollow.
*At 99 speed, Brollow is the second-fastest character in the game, beating all [[Cat Units]] and only losing to [[Assassin Bear]]'s 150.
*Brollow and his variants appear in gimmick stages where they are spammed if the enemy base is not  destroyed in one hit. Each of these stages is in a different [[Legend Stages]] campaign: Stories of Legend has [[Cubist Crimes]] with Brollow, Uncanny Legends has [[Tear-Soaked Puppy]] with [[Zollow]], and Zero Legends has [[Wicked Clergyman]] with Diabrollow.

